 "source": "Example 12.6 of Power System Stability and Control (McGraw-Hill, 1994), pp. 813-814, Figure E12.8: two similar areas joined by a weak tie (two circuits of 2 x 110 km between buses 7, 8, 9), four units of 900 MVA, 20 kV, step-up transformers j0.15 pu on 900 MVA, lines r = 0.0001, x = 0.001, b = 0.00175 pu/km on 100 MVA and 230 kV, the loads and the shunt capacitors of buses 7 and 9, area 1 exporting 400 MW; 60 Hz. G3 is the slack bus at 1.03 pu, -6.8 deg. The dynamic data of the units are pcl.rms.TWO_AREA_UNIT (pcl.rms.two_area_machines). Generators: x\"d = 0.25 pu is the subtransient reactance of the example; cos phi = 0.9 is a typical value for the short circuit, not part of it."
